##
    Blocks closed with the wrong word.

    This program does not compile. Every block says what it closes, and the compiler checks
    the qualifier — so a mismatched closer names both the word written and the construct it
    fails to match, rather than reporting a missing brace somewhere near the end of the file.
##

shared model Program
    function Main()
        boolean ready = true;

        if ready
            Console.WriteLine("yes");
        end loop

        loop while ready
            ready = false;
        end if
    end function
end model
